SIGNIFICANT CHANGES FROM UPSTREAM

Sweetly Lyrics Overlay retains Spicy Lyrics' renderer, animation system, styling
and lyrics-application code substantially unmodified, and changes the following:

  * Host platform. Upstream runs as a Spicetify extension inside the Spotify
    desktop client. This work runs as a standalone Electron application on
    macOS, adding src/main/, src/preload/ and src/renderer/.

  * Player source. Upstream reads playback state from Spicetify.Player. This
    work reads it from Apple Music via an AppleScript bridge, adapted through
    src/renderer/adapter/AppleMusicPlayer.ts, which implements the same export
    surface as upstream's src/components/Global/SpotifyPlayer.ts.

  * Lyrics sourcing. This work adds src/main/lyrics/, providing its own
    provider chain, track matching, and a local forced-alignment pipeline
    (scripts/align_lyrics.py) for generating word-level timings.

  * Custom lyrics storage. Upstream stores user-supplied TTML in IndexedDB.
    This work stores it on the filesystem under ~/.sweetly-custom/ so that the
    alignment pipeline and the user interface share a single location.

Files under `src/` other than `main/`, `preload/` and `renderer/` are upstream
Spicy Lyrics code. Modifications are kept minimal and local so they remain
visible via `diff` against the upstream repository.

